          one disadvantage of using Jenkins for  CD 
                - Is that you need to give it your credentials which is a security risk
                - since is installed outside the cluster is has no visibility of the cluster and will not know if the deployment succeeded or not 
                  (except you configure a slack notification)
                - Jenkins does not have visibility of the git repo and will not be able to watch the git repo (except you configure a slack notification) 
                  wheras a Tool like Argo is installed inside the cluster and can whatch over the cluster and helps reconcile the current state of the 
                  cluster with the manifest file

               key noted for jenkins pipe
         1 - your source code repo should be diff from your manifest file repo (deployment, services, etc)
         2 - ensure that you install the reconcilers in our cluster ==ArgoCD (it used a push mechanism) .after a commit or push on github it will be notifies after 3 min 
             fluxCd used a pull mechanism = it watches your repo and goes to pull each time there's a commit
         3 - write APP config file for ArgoCD : 
                ==source = repo (put the url of our git repo)
                ==Destination= cluster

